# /tests/usertest — programs-surface test orchestrator.
#
# One-shot: exits cleanly on completion; svcmgr never restarts it. The
# orchestrator compares /tests/programs/ with TESTERS, the testers the image
# holds, failing for each one named and absent or present and unnamed; spawns
# each named one present, sequentially, killing one still running after
# TESTER_BOUND_MS; then powers off via the pwrmgr.shutdown seed. A new tester
# is added to TESTERS. The bound is 2.6 times the slowest tester's worst pass
# (pipestress, 46 s on riscv64 debug); with the 5 s drain after a kill it is
# the added bound the usertest CI cells' budgets are derived with, so a change
# to it re-derives them (programs/usertest/README.md § Testers).
#
# The later seeds are authorities testers take: TESTER_SEEDS names, per
# tester, the seed slots usertest hands it as its bootstrap caps (slot 0,
# pwrmgr.shutdown, is usertest's own). The hello tester takes pwrmgr.deny to
# check the delivery; the crashme tester takes crashd.core, the authority to
# ask the crash service for a live core (services/crashd/docs/operation.md
# § Live Core). See docs/testing.md § Per-program tester protocol.
#
# Recipe lives under /config/svcmgr/tests/, which svcmgr does NOT scan.
# To enable in a boot, copy this file into /config/svcmgr/services/
# between `cargo xtask build` and `cargo xtask run`. See docs/testing.md.
binary    = /tests/usertest
priority  = 10
sched_max = 10
argv      = usertest
restart   = never
critical  = no
namespace = universal
cwd       = /data
env       = TESTERS=crashme;deadline;debugger;hello;pipestress;shell;stdiotest;threadchurn;threadstack TESTER_BOUND_MS=120000 TESTER_SEEDS=hello:1;crashme:2
seed      = pwrmgr.shutdown pwrmgr.deny crashd.core
